    "text": "One of the worst döner I’ve had in Berlin.\n\nHonestly, everything was disappointing; from the bread to the salad. What made the experience even worse was the incredibly slow service. I went there around midnight, with only five people ahead of me, and there were three employees working. Somehow, it still took around 30 minutes to prepare a single döner.\n\nThe staff spent a lot of time talking to customers or among themselves while orders were being prepared at an unbelievably slow pace. It felt like there was absolutely no sense of urgency.\n\nFor €7.90, this is simply not worth it. The food was poor, the service was painfully slow, and the overall experience was frustrating. Definitely not a place I would recommend.",
    "textTranslated": null
  },
